Options -Indexes
DirectorySlash Off

RewriteEngine On

# Highest precedence: /signal and /signal/ both serve signal.html. Without this,
# LiteSpeed sees the signal/ directory and 301-redirects /signal → /signal/, which
# then 403s because Options -Indexes blocks directory listing. Two rules cover
# both with-slash and without-slash entry points.
RewriteRule ^signal/?$ signal.html [NC,L]

# IC workshop June 25 (2026-06-12): registration page lives at /workshop/.
# Serve the directory index explicitly (DirectorySlash Off would otherwise
# send /workshop into the clean-URL rule and 404 on workshop.html).
#
# 2026-07-31: same latent bug as /kit (see reference_trailing_slash_breaks_
# relative_links_2026_07_30.md) -- DirectorySlash Off served the no-slash
# form in place with no redirect, leaving document.baseURI at /workshop and
# breaking every relative href on the page. 301 to the slashed form first.
RewriteRule ^workshop$ /workshop/ [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^workshop/?$ workshop/index.html [NC,L]

# The ONLINE session page (Wednesday 2026-08-19, 11:00 am Mountain, $25) lives at
# /online/. Deliberately a second page and not a second state on /workshop/: the
# two run at the same time on purpose, the online session feeding the in-person
# one on August 27.
#
# Same two-rule shape every other page here needs, and for the same reason.
# DirectorySlash Off (line 2) means the no-slash form would otherwise be served
# IN PLACE with no redirect, leaving document.baseURI at /online and breaking
# every relative href on the page. The 301 to the slashed form MUST stay ahead
# of the serve rule. It cannot loop: /online/ already has a trailing slash and
# never matches ^online$. QSA keeps the UTMs on a typed link carrying them.
RewriteRule ^online$ /online/ [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^online/?$ online/index.html [NC,L]

# Post-payment landing, the success_url on Stripe payment link
# plink_1U1CWwQWqcWWuBB0jgP2KmJT. Same slash treatment, same reason.
RewriteRule ^online/thank-you$ /online/thank-you/ [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^online/thank-you/?$ online/thank-you/index.html [NC,L]
# A/B variant B of the workshop page (paid/ad traffic landed here via /w/ads).
#
# 2026-08-04: RETIRED to a redirect. Every headline, price and date on this page
# is welded to July 30, an event that has happened. Nothing points here any more
# (w/ads now goes to /workshop/), so the only way to reach it is a bookmark or an
# old ad, and both deserve the live page rather than a sold-out past date.
# One rule covers the slashed and unslashed forms, so either is a single 301.
# The page file is untouched in the repo; deleting these two lines and restoring
# the two commented ones below brings it back exactly as it was.
#   RewriteRule ^workshop-b$ /workshop-b/ [R=301,L,QSA]
#   RewriteRule ^workshop-b/?$ workshop-b/index.html [NC,L]
#
# 2026-08-07: widened to the explicit index.html form. /workshop-b/index.html was
# returning 200 and rendering the July 30 $47 variant, verified live before this
# change. Same closed hole as /ai-checklist/ and /seat/. No Stripe object touched.
RewriteRule ^workshop-b(/index\.html)?/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=legacy&utm_medium=redirect&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=legacy_workshop_b [NC,R=301,L]

# IC lead-magnet opt-in (free AI checklist) lives at /ai-checklist/.
# Same directory-index pattern as /workshop. Captures cold Meta-ad traffic.
#
# 2026-07-30: found while fixing the same defect on /kit. This page carries one
# relative reference, assets/cw-logo.png, which only resolves when the document
# base ends in a slash. Served in place at /ai-checklist the logo 404s and the
# page renders without its mark. Every /w/ short link already sends traffic to
# the slash form, so this only ever hit someone typing the URL, and the opt-in
# form and its Stripe target are absolute so nothing on the money path was
# affected. The 301 must stay ahead of the serve rule. It cannot loop:
# /ai-checklist/ has a trailing slash and never matches ^ai-checklist$. QSA
# keeps the UTMs on a typed link carrying them.
#
# 2026-08-04: RETIRED to a redirect, same reason as /workshop-b above. This page
# says "July 30" four times and offers a free seat at an event that is over. It
# was the destination of all sixteen short links until today; anyone holding an
# old link, printed card or newsletter now lands on the permanent page instead.
# Restoring it is deleting the redirect and uncommenting these two:
#   RewriteRule ^ai-checklist$ /ai-checklist/ [R=301,L,QSA]
#   RewriteRule ^ai-checklist/?$ ai-checklist/index.html [NC,L]
# Note this leaves the site with no live lead magnet. If the checklist is wanted
# as an evergreen magnet it needs its July 30 copy stripped first, which is a
# rewrite of the page, not a routing change.
#
# 2026-08-07: the pattern is widened to cover the explicit index.html form. The
# ^ai-checklist/?$ rule above matched the canonical URL only, so
# /ai-checklist/index.html fell straight through to the file and served the live
# "Claim my free seat $0" page unredirected -- confirmed with a 200 against the
# live host before this change. Free-seat copy is a standing defect on its own
# now (no free workshops unless Boubacar names one; August 19 is $25 and
# August 27 is $50), so the hole is closed the same way the July 16 page's was.
# 2026-08-17: now a 404, not a redirect, on Boubacar's standing instruction to
# take the free-seat pages offline and KEEP THE FILES ("404 the free seat pages
# but do not delete the pages as we may re-use them for other things"). He gave
# that instruction over a week ago; the 08-04/08-07 passes only redirected.
#
# RETIRED PAGE: "Claim your free seat | July 30 AI workshop, Sandy UT" -- H1 "A
# limited number of free seats to the July 30 workshop", CTA "Claim my free seat
# $0" wired to buy.stripe.com/dRm4gB4Tt8ZQ1IY2wBgEg0k (plink_1TtUuGQWqcWWuBB0
# 5dFBgLDD, unit_amount 0, INACTIVE in Stripe -- rendered "The link is no longer
# active." in a real browser 2026-08-17, screenshot in this commit's PR notes).
# Retired 2026-08-17. File KEPT at ai-checklist/index.html.
#
# 404 and not a redirect, deliberately: a 301 to /workshop/ takes someone who
# clicked for a free seat and lands them on a $50 checkout. That is a bait and
# switch, and it is the defect this change closes, not just a stale date. Same
# reasoning already applied to /free-thank-you/ on 08-07. A 404 is the honest
# answer to a page that no longer exists as an offer.
#
# RESTORING (do not, without checking free-seat copy is allowed again -- both
# current sessions are paid): delete the 404 rule below and put these back:
#   RewriteRule ^ai-checklist$ /ai-checklist/ [R=301,L,QSA]
#   RewriteRule ^ai-checklist/?$ ai-checklist/index.html [NC,L]
# The 301-before-serve shape in those two lines is load-bearing: DirectorySlash
# Off (line 2) serves the no-slash form IN PLACE, leaving document.baseURI at
# /ai-checklist and breaking the page's relative assets/cw-logo.png reference.
# The page's July 30 copy has to be rewritten before it can serve again anyway.
RewriteRule ^ai-checklist(/index\.html)?/?$ - [NC,R=404,L]
# IC simple one-screen QR conversion page (StartFEST + /w/ss) lived at /seat/.
#
# 2026-08-04: RETIRED to a redirect, same reason again. It renders a $47
# "Reserve my seat" CTA wired to the July 30 Stripe link, which would now take
# real money for a session that has already run. That makes it the most urgent
# of the three to retire, not the least.
# The rule matches ^seat/?$ only, so /seat/thank-you/ and /seat/assets/* are
# untouched. That matters: thank-you is a Stripe return URL and must keep
# resolving for anyone completing an older checkout.
# Restoring: delete the redirect, uncomment these two:
#   RewriteRule ^seat$ /seat/ [R=301,L,QSA]
#   RewriteRule ^seat/?$ seat/index.html [NC,L]
#
# 2026-08-07: widened to the explicit index.html form for the same reason as
# /ai-checklist/ above -- /seat/index.html was returning 200 and rendering the
# $47 July 30 CTA, verified live before this change. The Stripe link behind that
# CTA (plink_1TgCDE..., $47) is already INACTIVE in Stripe, so the page could
# only dead-end a clicker on a Stripe error. No Stripe object was touched here.
# The pattern still matches ^seat, ^seat/ and ^seat/index.html ONLY:
# /seat/thank-you/ (an ACTIVE Stripe return URL for the $50 and $25 links),
# /seat/aug19-credit/ and /seat/assets/* are all untouched.
RewriteRule ^seat(/index\.html)?/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=legacy&utm_medium=redirect&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=legacy_seat [NC,R=301,L]

# /seat/aug19-credit/ was the unlisted closed-list checkout for the August 19
# online attendees: the same August 27 seat at $25 instead of $50, because their
# online payment came off it.
#
# 2026-08-06: RETIRED, on Boubacar's explicit instruction, the same instruction
# that took the promise off /online/ earlier today ("remove the public promise of
# the $25 off so we can work that out one by one"). He is deciding the offer
# separately. This page is not a page that CARRIED the promise, it IS the
# promise: the headline, the lead, the ticket cell, the button and the closing
# line are all the credit and nothing else. Strip it and what is left is an
# unexplained $25 seat for August 27, publicly reachable by URL, undercutting the
# live $50 page it sits beside, with no reason on it for the difference. That is
# worse than no page, so the route comes out rather than the copy.
#
# Redirect and not a 404 because someone may hold the link. /online/ is the right
# landing: it is the page for the very session these people are in.
#
# The page file itself is DELETED in this same commit, not left on disk. Every
# other retirement in this file leaves its HTML in place and only unhooks the
# canonical URL, which is fine for a stale date but not for a live promise that
# checkout is not currently set up to keep. Nothing carrying it stays on the
# server. The rule below covers the slashed, unslashed and explicit index.html
# forms for the same reason.
#
# RESTORING (do not, without his say-so AND the offer settled):
#   git checkout f10eed1 -- seat/aug19-credit/index.html
# then delete the redirect and put these two back:
#   RewriteRule ^seat/aug19-credit$ /seat/aug19-credit/ [R=301,L,QSA]
#   RewriteRule ^seat/aug19-credit/?$ seat/aug19-credit/index.html [NC,L]
# The 301-before-serve shape in those two lines is load-bearing, not decoration:
# DirectorySlash Off (line 2) serves the no-slash form IN PLACE, which leaves
# document.baseURI at /seat/aug19-credit and breaks the page's relative
# references (reference_trailing_slash_breaks_relative_links_2026_07_30.md).
#
# Safe to sit after the ^seat/?$ redirect above: that pattern matches ^seat/?$
# and nothing else, so it never sees this path. It cannot loop either, because
# the target is /online/ and matches nothing here.
RewriteRule ^seat/aug19-credit(/index\.html)?/?$ /online/?utm_source=legacy&utm_medium=redirect&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_online_0819&utm_content=retired_credit_seat [NC,R=301,L]

# The July 30 attendee take-home kit lives at /kit/. This is the QR target
# printed on the cards and shown on the closing slide, so both the with-slash
# and without-slash forms have to resolve: DirectorySlash Off would otherwise
# send /kit into the clean-URL rule and 404 on kit.html.
#
# 2026-07-30: /kit and /kit/ both resolved, but only one of them WORKED.
# Serving the no-slash form in place left the document base at /kit, so every
# relative href on the page resolved against the site root instead of the kit
# directory: "Read the deck" went to /deck.html and "The one page cheat sheet"
# to /handout.html, both 404, and the slides PDF, the skill zip and the
# service worker registration went the same way, which silently killed the
# offline support this page depends on at the venue. The 301 below sends the
# no-slash form to the canonical directory URL BEFORE the page renders, so the
# base is right and the relative links land where they were always meant to.
# It must stay ahead of the serve rule, and it cannot loop: /kit/ has a
# trailing slash and so never matches ^kit$.
RewriteRule ^kit$ /kit/ [R=301,L]
RewriteRule ^kit/?$ kit/index.html [NC,L]
# The first draft of the kit page, kept at /kit-v1/ so the difference between
# what came out first and what shipped can be put on a screen side by side. It
# is linked from nowhere and carries noindex; it is opened by URL only. Same
# 301-then-serve shape as /kit above, for the same reason: served in place, the
# no-slash form would leave the base at /kit-v1 and break the page's own links.
RewriteRule ^kit-v1$ /kit-v1/ [R=301,L]
RewriteRule ^kit-v1/?$ kit-v1/index.html [NC,L]
# Customer-facing support + privacy pages (Stripe links point here). Same
# directory-index pattern as /workshop: DirectorySlash Off would otherwise send
# /support and /privacy into the clean-URL rule and 404 on support.html.
# 2026-07-31: same trailing-slash defect as /kit on all three -- 301 to the
# slashed form first so document.baseURI is correct before relative links resolve.
RewriteRule ^support$ /support/ [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^support/?$ support/index.html [NC,L]
RewriteRule ^privacy$ /privacy/ [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^privacy/?$ privacy/index.html [NC,L]
RewriteRule ^terms$ /terms/ [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^terms/?$ terms/index.html [NC,L]
# SW cold-email link consistency (2026-07-15): signature shows
# catalystworks.consulting/geolisted so recipients see one CW domain.
# Send them straight through to the geolisted.co landing page.
RewriteRule ^geolisted/?$ https://geolisted.co/ [R=301,L]
# /free-thank-you/ was the $0 Stripe checkout success page: the after_completion
# redirect target of the free-seat payment link, confirming "your free seat is
# saved" for July 30.
#
# 2026-08-07: TAKEN OFFLINE, on Boubacar's explicit instruction. Both August
# sessions are paid -- August 19 online is $25, August 27 in person at SLCC
# Miller Campus is $50 -- and a live page telling a visitor a $0 seat is saved
# contradicts the whole offer. It was still returning 200 on every form,
# including the explicit /free-thank-you/index.html, verified against the live
# host before this change.
#
# It is a 404, not a 301, and that is deliberate. Every other retired page here
# is a LANDING page, where an old link should land on the live offer, so those
# redirect to /workshop/. This one is a CONFIRMATION page: redirecting it would
# take someone who was told their free seat is saved and drop them on a $50
# sales page, which reads worse than the page simply being gone. Nothing links
# to it (repo-wide grep: one code comment, no href), it is absent from
# sitemap.xml, and it already carried noindex,nofollow. The 404 is what takes
# it out of any index that still holds it.
#
# The file is NOT deleted. free-thank-you/index.html stays in the repo exactly
# as it was, per the instruction to keep it in the records while making it
# publicly unreachable. Only the route comes out.
#
# Safe because nothing can still arrive here: the ONLY payment link on the whole
# Stripe account whose after_completion redirect points at this URL is
# plink_1TtUuGQWqcWWuBB05dFBgLDD ("AI Workshop - Free Seat (July 30, Sandy UT)",
# unit_amount 0), and it was already INACTIVE before this change. Verified by
# listing all 25 payment links on the account (has_more:false) with their
# after_completion redirect URLs and amounts -- it is also the only $0 link that
# exists. No Stripe object was created, changed or deactivated by this commit.
#
# RESTORING (do not, without checking free-seat copy is allowed again):
# delete the 404 rule below and put these two back:
#   RewriteRule ^free-thank-you$ /free-thank-you/ [R=301,L,QSA]
#   RewriteRule ^free-thank-you/?$ free-thank-you/index.html [NC,L]
RewriteRule ^free-thank-you(/index\.html)?/?$ - [NC,R=404,L]
# /free-workshop-july16/ was the CANCELLED July 16 free session's live capture
# page: a working form, still POSTing real leads to workshop-register, still
# confirming a $0 seat for a date and event ("free session, July 16, 7:00 to
# 8:30pm") over three weeks past.
#
# 2026-08-07: the file is DELETED in this same commit, not left on disk. The
# old rule here only unhooked the canonical ^free-workshop-july16/?$ URL, which
# left the explicit index.html form -- /free-workshop-july16/index.html --
# reachable and serving the live page unredirected, same gap the aug19-credit
# retirement below calls out. That gap is a bigger problem on this page than
# most: it is not just a stale date, it is a still-collecting $0 offer, and
# free-seat copy is now a standing defect on its own regardless of the date
# (see the no-free-workshops rule). Same reasoning as aug19-credit: this page
# does not carry the promise, it IS the promise, so the route comes out and the
# file goes with it. Redirect and not a 404 because an old SBDC-newsletter link
# may still be out there; /workshop/ is the live permanent page, same target
# this rule already used before the file was deleted. The rule below covers
# the slashed, unslashed and explicit index.html forms, same pattern as
# aug19-credit.
#
# RESTORING (do not, without checking free-seat copy is allowed again):
#   git checkout 3c909d4 -- free-workshop-july16/index.html
# then delete the redirect below and put this back:
#   RewriteRule ^free-workshop-july16/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=sbdc&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=stale_july16_redirect [R=301,L]
# 2026-08-17: now a 404, not a redirect, same standing instruction as
# /ai-checklist/ above.
#
# RETIRED PAGE: the CANCELLED July 16 free session's $0 capture page. Its route
# was retired and its FILE DELETED 2026-08-07 (restore with
# `git checkout 3c909d4 -- free-workshop-july16/index.html`), so this rule now
# only unhooks a path with nothing behind it. Retired-as-404 2026-08-17.
#
# 404 and not a 301 for the same bait-and-switch reason: an old SBDC-newsletter
# link promising a free session should not land on a $50 checkout. /w/july16, the
# short link that fed this page, is 404'd in the same commit.
#
# RESTORING (do not, without checking free-seat copy is allowed again): restore
# the file per the git checkout above, then delete the 404 rule and put back:
#   RewriteRule ^free-workshop-july16/?$ free-workshop-july16/index.html [NC,L]
RewriteRule ^free-workshop-july16(/index\.html)?/?$ - [NC,R=404,L]
# The July 30 comp-seat RSVP page booked NOTHING (Beehiiv-only) yet told
# visitors "your seat is held" -- a false claim. Repoint to the live free-seat
# capture that actually reserves the $0 seat. Organic medium keeps attribution
# honest. NOTE: /w/vip below still resolves here via a second 301 hop.
#
# 2026-08-07: widened to the explicit index.html form. /rsvp-0730/index.html was
# returning 200 and rendering the live "$0, no card" comp-seat page for July 30,
# verified live before this change -- the same free-seat defect as
# /ai-checklist/index.html, on a page that also fires a Purchase pixel event for
# a $0 seat. Same fix, same shape as the July 16 retirement.
# 2026-08-17: now a 404, not a redirect, same standing instruction and same
# reasoning as /ai-checklist/ above.
#
# RETIRED PAGE: the July 30 comp-seat RSVP page -- "$0, no card" free comp seat,
# and it also fires a Purchase pixel event for that $0 seat. Retired 2026-08-17.
# File KEPT at rsvp-0730/index.html.
#
# 404 and not a 301 for the bait-and-switch reason: this page's entire promise is
# a free seat with no card, so sending its clicker to a $50 checkout is worse
# than the page being gone. /w/vip, the 1:1 comp link that used to reach this
# page's offer, is 404'd in the same commit for the same reason.
#
# RESTORING (do not, without checking free-seat copy is allowed again): delete
# the 404 rule below and put these back:
#   RewriteRule ^rsvp-0730$ /rsvp-0730/ [R=301,L,QSA]
#   RewriteRule ^rsvp-0730/?$ rsvp-0730/index.html [NC,L]
RewriteRule ^rsvp-0730(/index\.html)?/?$ - [NC,R=404,L]
# Services offer-ladder page lives at /services/ (unlinked preview, awaiting nav sign-off).
# 2026-07-31: same trailing-slash defect as /kit -- 301 to the slashed form first.
RewriteRule ^services$ /services/ [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^services/?$ services/index.html [NC,L]
# 5-Day Bottleneck Audit landing page lives at /bottleneck-audit/ (unlinked preview, awaiting nav sign-off).
# Same trailing-slash defect + fix as /services above.
RewriteRule ^bottleneck-audit$ /bottleneck-audit/ [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^bottleneck-audit/?$ bottleneck-audit/index.html [NC,L]
# Short link for the lead-magnet (Meta ads + any channel): /w/start -> opt-in page.
# Campaign = stable magnet base; utm_content carries the current cohort for per-run segmentation.
RewriteRule ^w/start/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=meta&utm_medium=paid&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=meta_leadmagnet [R=301,L,QSA]

# Workshop short links: one per channel, UTM baked behind the 301.
# Never reuse a slug across campaigns.
# 2026-07-27: the July 30 workshop stays FREE through the event (2026-07-25
# decision), so every partner slug below that still pointed at /workshop/ (the
# $47 flow) was sending a partner's audience to a paid page for a free event.
# Repointed to /ai-checklist/, the live free-seat capture, matching w/li's shape.
# Each slug keeps its own utm_source + utm_content so per-partner attribution
# survives; slugs that carried no utm_content got a meaningful one rather than
# collapsing into an unattributable blob. Same "track_free" prohibition applies:
# /workshop/ and /workshop-b/ attribute the paid split test with
# /track_free/.test(utm_content), so no value here may contain that substring.
RewriteRule ^w/svc/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=chamber&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=south_valley [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^w/sjc/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=chamber&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=south_jordan [R=301,L,QSA]
# 2026-07-21 (Boubacar, explicit): the organic LinkedIn + X push for July 30 goes
# to the FREE seat capture, not the $47 page. Both were pointed at /workshop/,
# which is the paid flow. Repointed to /ai-checklist/, the live free-seat page.
# utm_medium=organic because these are hand-posted, not an ad buy (same reason
# w/fb-organic exists). utm_content MUST NOT contain "track_free" -- /workshop/
# and /workshop-b/ attribute the paid split test with /track_free/.test(utm_content),
# so "organic_li" / "organic_x" keep organic clicks out of the paid free-first arm.
RewriteRule ^w/li/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=organic_li [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^w/x/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=x&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=organic_x [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^w/nl/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=newsletter [R=301,L,QSA]

# ---- ONLINE SESSION (2026-08-19) short links, minted 2026-08-05 ----
# FRESH slugs on a FRESH campaign key. Every w/* slug above carries
# utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent after the 2026-08-04 sweep moved all
# sixteen of them onto it, so reusing any of them would fold this session's
# numbers into the in-person page's. These four are the only ones tagged
# ic_workshop_online_0819 and they are the only ones that point at /online/.
RewriteRule ^w/online/?$ /online/?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=link&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_online_0819&utm_content=direct_online [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^w/online-li/?$ /online/?utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_online_0819&utm_content=organic_li [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^w/online-x/?$ /online/?utm_source=x&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_online_0819&utm_content=organic_x [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^w/online-nl/?$ /online/?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_online_0819&utm_content=newsletter [R=301,L,QSA]

# ---- FRACTIONAL RETAINER short links, minted 2026-08-12 ----
# The retainer is a different offer from the workshops, so these carry their own
# campaign key (fractional_retainer) rather than any ic_workshop_* key. Folding
# them into a workshop campaign would make retainer clicks unreadable next to
# seat sales. Own namespace (fx/) for the same reason: every w/* slug means
# workshop. Default target is /fractional/ai/ because the AI side is the one the
# newsletter and the organic posts lead with; the HR page has its own -hr slugs.
# These are clean of internal names and safe to put in front of a subscriber,
# which the tracked booking redirect on the api hostname is not.
RewriteRule ^fx/?$ /fractional/ai/?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=link&utm_campaign=fractional_retainer&utm_content=direct [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^fx/nl/?$ /fractional/ai/?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=fractional_retainer&utm_content=newsletter [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^fx/li/?$ /fractional/ai/?utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=fractional_retainer&utm_content=organic_li [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^fx/x/?$ /fractional/ai/?utm_source=x&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=fractional_retainer&utm_content=organic_x [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^fx/hr/?$ /fractional/hr/?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=link&utm_campaign=fractional_retainer&utm_content=direct_hr [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^fx/hr-nl/?$ /fractional/hr/?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=fractional_retainer&utm_content=newsletter_hr [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^fx/hr-li/?$ /fractional/hr/?utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=fractional_retainer&utm_content=organic_li_hr [R=301,L,QSA]
# SPLIT TEST (July 30 workshop) -- two paid Meta tracks under one campaign,
# distinguished by utm_content so seats are attributable per track.
# Track 1 DIRECT: was cold ad -> $47 seat page (variant B). 2026-07-27: repointed
# to the free capture with the rest (see RESTORE NOTE at the bottom of this file).
# The ad set is paused at $0/day, so the split test is not actively running and
# nothing is being corrupted mid-flight. utm_content=track_direct is preserved so
# the track stays distinguishable when the paid destination is restored.
RewriteRule ^w/ads/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=meta&utm_medium=paid&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=track_direct [R=301,L,QSA]
# Track 2 FREE-FIRST: cold ad -> free AI checklist (email capture + Meta Lead)
# then its built-in CTA to the $47 July 30 seat. utm_content=track_free.
#
# 2026-08-17: RETIRED SHORT LINK, now a 404. Same standing instruction as the
# free-seat pages above. This slug's whole meaning is "free": it was the
# free-first arm of the July 30 Meta split test, and its own utm_content says
# track_free. Pointing a link a reader believes is free at the $50 page is the
# bait and switch this pass closes, and it is a worse offence on a short link
# than on a page, because the reader cannot see the destination before clicking.
# Nothing on the site links to it; only an old ad or a saved link reaches it, and
# the ad set behind it is paused at $0/day.
#
# RESTORING (do not, without a free offer Boubacar has named): delete the 404
# rule and put this back:
#   RewriteRule ^w/free/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=meta&utm_medium=paid&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=track_free [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^w/free/?$ - [NC,R=404,L]
RewriteRule ^w/fb/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=facebook&utm_medium=paid&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=fb_ad [R=301,L,QSA]

# ORGANIC free-seat link -- for a hand-posted FB/social post, NOT an ad buy.
# Exists because every /w/ free-seat slug above bakes utm_medium=paid: sharing
# one in an organic post logs the click as paid Meta traffic and corrupts the
# ad-spend read. This is the attribution-honest slug for anything Boubacar
# posts by hand.
# utm_content MUST NOT contain the substring "track_free": /workshop/ and
# /workshop-b/ attribute the split test with /track_free/.test(utm_content),
# so a value like "track_free_organic" would silently register organic clicks
# as the paid free-first arm. "organic_fb" cannot match, which is the point.
RewriteRule ^w/fb-organic/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=facebook&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=organic_fb [R=301,L,QSA]

# Paid-seat counterpart to /w/free. Direct/hand-shared attribution, no channel
# baked in. 2026-07-27: repointed to the free capture with the rest. This slug is
# hand-shareable, so while the July 30 workshop is free it was the likeliest way
# for someone to hit a $47 checkout for a free event. utm_content=direct_paid is
# preserved unchanged so restoring is a destination swap, nothing else.
RewriteRule ^w/paid/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=link&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=direct_paid [R=301,L,QSA]

# Same 2026-07-27 free-event repoint as the chamber slugs above. w/ss pointed at
# /seat/, which renders a $47 "Reserve my seat" CTA wired to the paid Stripe
# link, so it was a paid destination too despite not being /workshop/.
RewriteRule ^w/sbdc/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=sbdc&utm_medium=partner&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=sbdc_partner [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^w/beccy/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=beccy&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=beccy [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^w/ss/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=silicon_slopes&utm_medium=event&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=silicon_slopes [R=301,L,QSA]

# Old SBDC-newsletter short link for the CANCELLED July 16 free session. Its old
# target (/free-workshop-july16/) now 301s to the live July 30 free-seat capture;
# point this straight there too so a straggler clicking the old newsletter link
# lands on the working capture in a single hop, not a double 301.
#
# 2026-08-17: RETIRED SHORT LINK, now a 404. Same standing instruction and same
# bait-and-switch reasoning as /w/free above: this slug was minted for a
# CANCELLED FREE session, so a straggler clicking it from the old SBDC
# newsletter believes they are claiming a free seat. Its old destination
# (/free-workshop-july16/) is itself a 404 as of this commit.
#
# RESTORING (do not, without a free offer Boubacar has named): delete the 404
# rule and put this back:
#   RewriteRule ^w/july16/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=sbdc&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=stale_july16_shortlink [R=301,L]
RewriteRule ^w/july16/?$ - [NC,R=404,L]

# DISCRETE comp-seat link for July 30 -- Boubacar shares this 1:1 only (never
# posted publicly, never linked from the paid page). Confirms a free seat with
# NO Stripe charge.
# 2026-07-27: was /rsvp-0730/, which itself 301s to /ai-checklist/. That second
# hop carries its own query string and no QSA, so the comp UTMs were silently
# discarded and overwritten with stale_rsvp0730_redirect -- comp seats were not
# separable from organic in the data. Collapsed to a single hop straight to the
# same final page, which strictly preserves MORE attribution than before rather
# than trading any away. Same single-hop treatment w/july16 already got.
# "track_comp" cannot match /track_free/, so it stays out of the paid free-first arm.
#
# 2026-08-17: RETIRED SHORT LINK, now a 404. Same standing instruction and same
# bait-and-switch reasoning as /w/free above. This is the comp-seat slug: its
# utm_medium is literally "comp" and its promise is a seat with NO charge, so a
# 1:1 recipient holding it believes they have a free seat. Sending them to the
# $50 page is the worst version of the switch, because it arrived as a personal
# invitation. Its old page (/rsvp-0730/) is a 404 as of this commit too. A comp
# seat is still available -- Boubacar gives it directly, one by one, which is the
# posture he already chose for the August 27 credit; it does not need a URL.
#
# RESTORING (do not, without a comp offer Boubacar has named): delete the 404
# rule and put this back:
#   RewriteRule ^w/vip/?$ /workshop/?utm_source=direct_invite&utm_medium=comp&utm_campaign=ic_workshop_permanent&utm_content=track_comp [R=301,L,QSA]
RewriteRule ^w/vip/?$ - [NC,R=404,L]

# Clean URLs: append .html for any path without an extension. Handles top-level
# (/governance → /governance.html), nested (/lens/throughput → /lens/throughput.html,
# /for/hvac → /for/hvac.html, /signal/issue-3 → /signal/issue-3.html), and arbitrary
# depth. The character class [^\.]+ matches across "/" because slashes are not dots.
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-f
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-d
RewriteRule ^([^\.]+)$ $1.html [NC,L]

# =====================================================================
# CURRENT ROUTING -- 2026-08-17 free-seat 404 sweep (Boubacar, standing
# instruction, given over a week before it was carried out)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# His words: "I already told you over a week ago to 404 the free seat pages but
# to not delete the pages as we may re-use them for other things."
#
# Every free-seat surface now returns 404 on the slashed, unslashed and explicit
# index.html forms. Every page FILE stays in the repo. Each rule above carries
# the exact lines to uncomment to bring its page back.
#
#   PAGES, now 404, files kept:
#     /ai-checklist/          "Claim my free seat $0", July 30
#     /rsvp-0730/             "$0, no card" comp-seat RSVP, July 30
#     /free-thank-you/        $0 checkout confirmation (already 404 since 08-07)
#     /free-workshop-july16/  cancelled July 16 free session (file deleted 08-07)
#
#   SHORT LINKS, now 404:
#     /w/free      free-first Meta arm, utm_content=track_free
#     /w/vip       1:1 comp seat, utm_medium=comp
#     /w/july16    cancelled July 16 FREE session, SBDC newsletter
#
# WHY 404 AND NOT THE 301 THESE ALREADY HAD. The 08-04 and 08-07 passes pointed
# all of them at /workshop/. That behaviour is itself the defect: a visitor who
# clicked for a FREE seat landed on a $50 checkout. A 404 is the honest answer
# and it is what he asked for. /free-thank-you/ was already reasoned this way on
# 08-07 and the same reasoning now covers the other six.
#
# NOT TOUCHED, on purpose:
#   /w/start   a lead-magnet slug, not a free-seat slug, and a separate lane is
#              live on the lead magnet right now. Flagged for Boubacar rather
#              than changed, because it still 301s to the $50 page and carries
#              the same read-a-free-thing-get-a-paid-page shape.
#   /seat/, /workshop-b/   PAID pages ($47), already retired-by-redirect. Not
#              free-seat surfaces, so out of this instruction's scope.
#   /w/svc /w/sjc /w/li /w/x /w/nl /w/ss /w/sbdc /w/beccy /w/ads /w/fb
#   /w/fb-organic /w/paid  generic per-channel slugs. They pointed at the free
#              capture only during the 07-27 free window; pointing at the live
#              paid page is correct for them now.
#
# NO STRIPE OBJECT WAS CREATED, CHANGED OR DEACTIVATED. The $0 payment link
# behind /ai-checklist/ (dRm4gB4Tt8ZQ1IY2wBgEg0k / plink_1TtUuGQWqcWWuBB05dFBgLDD,
# unit_amount 0) was verified INACTIVE on 2026-08-17 by opening it in a real
# browser: it renders "The link is no longer active." A 200 from buy.stripe.com
# is NOT evidence a link is live -- Stripe's checkout shell returns 200 and then
# renders that message, which is how this was mis-read as claimable earlier.
# =====================================================================
#
# =====================================================================
# CURRENT ROUTING -- 2026-08-04 post-event sweep
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# July 30 has happened. Every route that touched it now goes to /workshop/,
# the permanent page, which carries no date: it reads "next session being
# scheduled" until one is confirmed and shows the date once it is. That is
# the whole point of it, and it is why this should be the last sweep of
# this kind. A future session changes the date INSIDE that page. It does
# not get a new URL, and no rule below should ever be repointed again.
#
# Everything below now resolves to /workshop/ in exactly one 301:
#   all sixteen w/* slugs
#   /ai-checklist/, /seat/, /workshop-b/   (retired-by-redirect, file kept)
#   /rsvp-0730/, /free-workshop-july16/    (rsvp-0730 retired-by-redirect;
#                                            free-workshop-july16 retired
#                                            AND deleted 2026-08-07, see its
#                                            own rule above)
#   boubacarbarry.com/workshop/            (separate repo, meta-refresh)
#
# Each slug keeps its own utm_source, utm_medium and utm_content, so the
# per-channel split survives intact. utm_campaign is the one value that
# changed: ic_workshop_0730 and ic_workshop_leadmagnet both became
# ic_workshop_permanent. That was deliberate. Clicks arriving now belong to
# whatever session comes next, and counting them inside a campaign that
# closed on July 30 would quietly corrupt that campaign's numbers. The one
# other content change: w/start carried utm_content=cohort:2026_06_25, a
# June label that is simply false on August traffic.
#
# Of the retired pages, /ai-checklist/, /seat/, /workshop-b/ and /rsvp-0730/ are
# redirects, not deletions -- their files are still in the repo and each rule
# above carries the lines to uncomment if one is ever wanted back.
# /free-workshop-july16/ is the exception: it was a live $0 lead-capture form,
# not just a stale date, so 2026-08-07 deleted the file too (see its own rule
# above for why and how to restore it).
#
# 2026-08-07 free-surface sweep (Boubacar, explicit -- both August sessions are
# PAID, and free-seat copy is a defect on its own now):
#   /free-thank-you/   404, file kept. It is a confirmation page, not a landing
#                      page, so it does not redirect. See its own rule above.
#   /ai-checklist/     redirect pattern widened to cover /index.html
#   /rsvp-0730/        redirect pattern widened to cover /index.html
#   /seat/             redirect pattern widened to cover /index.html
#   /workshop-b/       redirect pattern widened to cover /index.html
# All four of those were still returning 200 on their explicit index.html form
# and serving the live page -- the same gap the July 16 retirement found. The
# only routes still serving a workshop page are /workshop/ (August 27, $50),
# /online/ (August 19, $25) and their two thank-you pages, which are ACTIVE
# Stripe return URLs and must keep resolving.
#
# No Stripe object was created, changed or deactivated in that sweep. The only
# $0 payment link on the account (plink_1TtUuG..., "AI Workshop - Free Seat
# (July 30, Sandy UT)") was already INACTIVE, and it is the only link anywhere
# whose after_completion redirect pointed at /free-thank-you/.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPERSEDED -- 2026-07-27 free-routing sweep (Boubacar, explicit)
# Kept because it explains where each slug's UTM values came from.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The July 30 workshop was FREE through the event, so EVERY workshop short
# link was repointed to /ai-checklist/ (the free-seat capture). The paid
# pages themselves were deliberately NOT touched and still worked:
# /workshop/, /workshop-b/ and /seat/ were all intact and reachable.
# This was a routing change only.
#
# The pre-07-27 destinations, for the record. Do NOT restore these: all
# three targets are welded to July 30 and two of them charge $47 for it.
#
#   w/svc    -> /workshop/     (was, pre 2026-07-27)
#   w/sjc    -> /workshop/
#   w/nl     -> /workshop/     (also had NO utm_content originally;
#                               utm_content=newsletter was ADDED 07-27)
#   w/sbdc   -> /workshop/     (also had NO utm_content originally;
#                               utm_content=sbdc_partner was ADDED 07-27)
#   w/beccy  -> /workshop/     (also had NO utm_content originally;
#                               utm_content=beccy was ADDED 07-27)
#   w/ss     -> /seat/         (paid: /seat/ renders a $47 CTA)
#   w/ads    -> /workshop-b/   (Meta split test, track DIRECT)
#   w/paid   -> /workshop/
#   w/vip    -> /rsvp-0730/    (do NOT blindly restore this one: the old
#                               target double-hopped and dropped the comp
#                               UTMs. It now goes straight to the final
#                               page in one hop. Restore only if comps
#                               need their own page again.)
#
# Already correct before the sweep, left alone, no restore needed:
#   w/li, w/x, w/free, w/fb, w/fb-organic, w/start, w/july16
#
# The "track_free" constraint that governed the old sweep is now dead, and
# it is worth saying why rather than leaving a stale warning in place. It
# existed because the old /workshop/ and /workshop-b/ pages branched on
# /track_free/.test(utm_content) to attribute the paid split test. The
# permanent /workshop/ page has no such branch, and /workshop-b/ no longer
# serves. So w/free may keep utm_content=track_free without side effects.
# =====================================================================

# Force browsers to revalidate HTML + CSS on every load so style/layout fixes
# propagate immediately rather than living in client caches for hours.
# Static assets (images, fonts) keep long TTL via default LiteSpeed behavior.
<FilesMatch "\.(html|htm|css)$">
  Header set Cache-Control "no-cache, must-revalidate, max-age=0"
</FilesMatch>
